From: egui-aros
Subject: [PATCH] eframe: run the AROS event loop with run_app and return from it

Crate: eframe 0.37.0 from storytold/egui 6d518fc799681571963842f95b55a6b68431b15a,
  manifest made standalone by scripts/ea.py.
Date: 2026-10-28 (rebased from the eframe 0.36.2 series of 2026-10-19)
Problem: eframe's default run mode (NativeOptions::run_and_return) and
  EframeWinitApplication::pump_eframe_app use winit's run_on_demand and
  pump_events extensions, which winit offers only on Windows, macOS,
  Android, X11 and Wayland. The AROS winit backend (contrib
  winit-0.30.13-aros.diff) has neither, so eframe does not compile.
  eframe's other mode, run_app, ends the process with
  std::process::exit(0) from inside the event loop when the window closes:
  run_native never returns, and winit's loop never frees its wake signal
  (AROS reports "returned with unfreed signal").
Rationale: the AROS backend's EventLoop::run returns when the loop exits.
  On AROS run_and_exit therefore builds its wrapper as for run_and_return
  (ask the loop to exit, keep the result) and returns that result, so
  run_native returns after the window has closed and the app's on_exit has
  run. The run-on-demand and pump paths are compiled out on AROS, as on iOS.
Scope: cfg gates of six items in native/run.rs, one re-export in lib.rs,
  and run_and_exit on AROS.
Upstream-status: candidate for the AROS contrib crate store (not submitted).
Limitations: run_native can be called only once per process on AROS (the
  thread-local loop reuse needs run_on_demand); pump_eframe_app and
  EframePumpStatus do not exist on AROS.
Prerequisites: 0001-aros-glutin-without-egl.patch.
Verification: see the egui-aros build records (branch egui-0.37). The first version of this
  patch (without the run_and_exit change) was run on pool v11-2 on
  2026-10-19 (runs g1-g3): the process ended inside the loop, as described.
Rebase: unchanged in content; 0.37 has the same six gates.
Removal: when the AROS winit backend implements run_on_demand.
---
diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 7fd9f3a..dc353df 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ pub use native::run::EframeWinitApplication;
 #[cfg(any(feature = "glow", feature = "wgpu_no_default_features"))]
 pub use native::viewport_hooks::ViewportHooks;
 
-#[cfg(not(any(target_arch = "wasm32", target_os = "ios")))]
+#[cfg(not(any(target_arch = "wasm32", target_os = "ios", target_os = "aros")))]
 #[cfg(any(feature = "glow", feature = "wgpu_no_default_features"))]
 pub use native::run::EframePumpStatus;
 
diff --git a/src/native/run.rs b/src/native/run.rs
index e42b458..4eef95e 100644
--- a/src/native/run.rs
+++ b/src/native/run.rs
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ fn create_event_loop(native_options: &mut epi::NativeOptions) -> Result<EventLoo
 ///
 /// We reuse the event-loop so we can support closing and opening an eframe window
 /// multiple times. This is just a limitation of winit.
-#[cfg(not(target_os = "ios"))]
+#[cfg(not(any(target_os = "ios", target_os = "aros")))]
 fn with_event_loop<R>(
     mut native_options: epi::NativeOptions,
     f: impl FnOnce(&mut EventLoop<UserEvent>, epi::NativeOptions) -> R,
@@ -430,7 +430,7 @@ impl<T: WinitApp> ApplicationHandler<UserEvent> for WinitAppWrapper<T> {
     }
 }
 
-#[cfg(not(target_os = "ios"))]
+#[cfg(not(any(target_os = "ios", target_os = "aros")))]
 fn run_and_return(event_loop: &mut EventLoop<UserEvent>, winit_app: impl WinitApp) -> Result {
     use winit::platform::run_on_demand::EventLoopExtRunOnDemand as _;
 
@@ -446,11 +446,18 @@ fn run_and_exit(event_loop: EventLoop<UserEvent>, winit_app: impl WinitApp) -> R
     log::trace!("Entering the winit event loop (run_app)…");
 
     // When to repaint what window
-    let mut app = WinitAppWrapper::new(winit_app, false);
+    // On AROS the loop returns when it exits (there is no run_on_demand to return from), so the
+    // wrapper asks it to exit instead of ending the process inside it.
+    let mut app = WinitAppWrapper::new(winit_app, cfg!(target_os = "aros"));
     event_loop.run_app(&mut app)?;
 
-    log::debug!("winit event loop unexpectedly returned");
-    Ok(())
+    #[cfg(target_os = "aros")]
+    return app.return_result;
+    #[cfg(not(target_os = "aros"))]
+    {
+        log::debug!("winit event loop unexpectedly returned");
+        Ok(())
+    }
 }
 
